Cell[TextData[{
 "or a partial expansion can be suppressed with ",
 StyleBox["Except",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " directive.  Name of option in our convention  generally should be a \
string, not a symbol. When processing options we, however, attempt to convert \
symbols to strings. When symbol is   Mathematica symbol (like in the case of ",
 StyleBox["Except",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ") it, therefore works (at least for simple options, i.e. options that dont\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]t include other options)."
}], "Text",
